    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0204" n="106" xml:id="pg106"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/1109: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-25T12:00:00+08:00">April 25,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received April 25—5:40 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>289. Legation’s 285, April 24, 3 p.m. Legation is telegraphing the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs the substance of Canton’s April 24, noon,<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d72-f1"/> and is urging upon him the importance of instructing the
                    authorities in Kwangtung and Kiangsi to cooperate in bringing relief to
                    foreigners in southern Kiangsi.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d72-f1" n="97" xml:id="d72-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram of even date from the Consul General at Canton to the Secretary of
                    State, <ref target="#pg104">p. 104</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
